lusion is false, the premise must be false. So, L must be false. That means the temperature is not very low. But does that mean the temperature is very high? Not necessarily. It could be moderate or just not very low. So, we can't conclude that the temperature is very high (option B). It just means it's not very low.\n\nOption C is about the wind being strong. None of the given statements mention anything about the wind. So, we can't infer anything about the wind from the given information.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the only thing we can definitively infer is that the sky is clear, which is option D.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D) The sky is clear.\n\n**Step-by-Step Explanation:**\n\n1. **Given Statements:**\n   - If reed flowers float (F), then Lin Xi goes (G). (F \u2192 G)\n   - If temperature is very low (L), then Lin Xi does not go (\u00acG). (L \u2192 \u00acG)\n   - Only when the sky is clear (C) did Lin Xi go. (G \u2192 C)\n\n2. **Known Fact:**\n   - Lin Xi went to see the reeds. (G is true)\n\n3. **Analyzing Each Statement:**\n   - From G \u2192 C, since G is true, C must be true. Therefore, the sky is clear.\n   - From F \u2192 G, G being true doesn't confirm F; F could be true or false.\n   - From L \u2192 \u00acG, since G is true, L must be false (temperature isn't very low), but it doesn't imply it's very high.\n   - No information about wind strength.\n\n**Conclusion:** Only option D can be inferred.\n\nThe correct option is: D",
