his is probably not related.\n\nSo, going back, the context presents a dilemma: the EU needs Turkey's cooperation but joining brings problems. So the conclusion should reflect that you can't have both. Option A says you can't have both full cooperation and avoid the problems, which fits. Option C says you can choose one or the other, but the context implies that getting cooperation means facing the problems, so it's not an either/or but rather a necessity to accept the problems if you want the cooperation. Therefore, Option A is the correct inference.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
