    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to solve this logic problem about mobile phone usage in an administrative department. Let me read through the context and the question again to make sure I understand everything.\n\nThe context has three points:\n\n1. Xiao Wang dialed the phone of everyone in the administrative department. So, Xiao Wang called every single person in the department. That means everyone, including Xiao Li and Xiao Zhao, received a call from Xiao Wang.\n\n2. Xiao Li once called Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao never called anyone else. So, Xiao Li made a call to Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao didn't make any other calls besides that. Wait, no, actually, it says Xiao Zhao never called anyone else, which might mean that Xiao Zhao only received calls but didn't make any, except maybe the one from Xiao Li? Or does it mean that Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else besides Xiao Li? Hmm, I think it means that Xiao Zhao didn't make any calls to others beyond Xiao Li, but actually, the way it's phrased is that Xiao Zhao never called anyone else. So, Xiao Zhao only received calls but didn't make any calls except perhaps to Xiao Li? Wait, no, Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao, so Xiao Zhao received a call from Xiao Li. But Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else, meaning Xiao Zhao didn't make any calls beyond that. So, Xiao Zhao only received a call from Xiao Li and didn't make any calls.\n\n3. People who have never answered calls from others in the administration department have never called others. So, if someone never answered a call from anyone else, then they themselves have never called anyone. This is a bit tricky. So, if someone has never answered a call (i.e., they never received a call that they answered), then they haven't called anyone. Alternatively, if someone has never answered a call from others, meaning they never picked up when someone called them, then they themselves have never made a call.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options can be inferred from the given information.\n\nLet's look at the options:\n\nA) Xiao Zhao never answered a phone call from Xiao Li.\n\nB) Xiao Li once answered a phone call from Xiao Wang.\n\nC) Someone in the administration department once called Xiao Wang.\n\nD) Xiao Wang answered the phone from everyone in the administration department.\n\nI need to figure out which of these must be true based on the given information.\n\nLet me break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, from point 1, Xiao Wang called everyone in the department. So, Xiao Wang made calls to Xiao Li, Xiao Zhao, and everyone else. So, Xiao Li and Xiao Zhao both received a call from Xiao Wang.\n\nFrom point 2, Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao, but Xiao Zhao never called anyone else. So, Xiao Zhao didn't make any calls beyond that. Wait, but Xiao Zhao received a call from Xiao Li, right? So, Xiao Zhao received two calls: one from Xiao Wang and one from Xiao Li. But Xiao Zhao didn't make any calls beyond that, meaning Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else except maybe Xiao Li? Wait, no, Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone else, so Xiao Zhao only received calls but didn't make any.\n\nWait, no, Xiao Zhao received a call from Xiao Li, but Xiao Zhao didn't make any calls. So, Xiao Zhao only received calls but didn't make any.\n\nNow, point 3 says that people who have never answered calls from others have never called others. So, if someone never answered a call (i.e., they never picked up when someone called them), then they themselves have never made a call.\n\nSo, let's see. Let's consider each person:\n\nXiao Wang: He called everyone, so he made calls. So, he must have answered calls because he made calls. Wait, no, the rule is about people who have never answered calls. So, if someone has never answered a call, they haven't called anyone. But Xiao Wang made calls, so he must have answered at least one call, because he made calls. Wait, no, that's not necessarily true. Because making a call doesn't mean you answered a call. Wait, but if you make a call, you might have received a call as well. Hmm, maybe I'm overcomplicating.\n\nLet me think about each person:\n\nXiao Wang: He called everyone, so he made calls. So, he must have answered calls because he made calls. Wait, no, that's not necessarily the case. He could have made calls without answering any. But according to point 3, if someone has never answered a call, they haven't called anyone. So, since Xiao Wang did call others, he must have answered at least one call. Because if he hadn't answered any calls, he wouldn't have called anyone, which contradicts point 1. So, Xiao Wang must have answered at least one call.\n\nXiao Li: She called Xiao Zhao, so she made a call. Therefore, according to point 3, she must have answered at least one call. Because if she hadn't answered any calls, she wouldn't have made any calls. So, Xiao Li must have answered at least one call.\n\nXiao Zhao: He didn't make any calls beyond receiving from Xiao Li. Wait, no, he didn't make any calls at all, because point 2 says he never called anyone else. So, Xiao Zhao didn't make any calls. Therefore, according to point 3, if someone hasn't called anyone, it's because they never answered a call. Wait, no, point 3 says that people who have never answered calls have never called others. So, the contrapositive is that if someone has called others, then they have answered at least one call. So, Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone, so it's possible that he never answered any calls, or he did answer some. But we don't know for sure.\n\nWait, but Xiao Zhao received calls from Xiao Wang and Xiao Li. So, he must have answered those calls, right? Because if he didn't answer, then the calls wouldn't have been completed. But the problem doesn't specify whether the calls were answered or not. It just says that Xiao Wang dialed everyone, and Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao. So, it's possible that Xiao Zhao didn't answer any of those calls. But according to point 3, if someone has never answered a call, they haven't called anyone. Since Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone, it's possible that he never answered any calls. But wait, he received calls from Xiao Wang and Xiao Li. So, if he didn't answer those, then he never answered any calls, which would mean he didn't call anyone, which is consistent. But if he did answer those calls, then he did answer calls, which is also possible.\n\nSo, we can't be sure whether Xiao Zhao answered the calls or not. But let's look at the options.\n\nOption A: Xiao Zhao never answered a phone call from Xiao Li. So, did Xiao Zhao answer Xiao Li's call? We don't know for sure. It's possible that he didn't answer, but it's also possible that he did. So, we can't infer this for sure.\n\nOption B: Xiao Li once answered a phone call from Xiao Wang. So, Xiao Wang called Xiao Li, as per point 1. Did Xiao Li answer that call? Well, according to point 3, since Xiao Li made a call (to Xiao Zhao), she must have answered at least one call. So, she must have answered at least one call. But the call from Xiao Wang is one possibility. So, it's possible that she answered Xiao Wang's call, but it's also possible that she answered someone else's call. However, since Xiao Wang called everyone, including Xiao Li, and Xiao Li must have answered at least one call, the only call she could have answered is from Xiao Wang, because she didn't receive any other calls except from Xiao Wang and Xiao Zhao. Wait, no, Xiao Zhao didn't make any calls, so Xiao Li only received a call from Xiao Wang. Therefore, the only call Xiao Li received was from Xiao Wang. So, since she must have answered at least one call, she must have answered Xiao Wang's call. Therefore, option B is correct.\n\nOption C: Someone in the administration department once called Xiao Wang. So, has anyone called Xiao Wang? We know that Xiao Wang called everyone, but did anyone call him? The information doesn't specify. Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao, and Xiao Zhao didn't call anyone. So, unless someone else called Xiao Wang, we don't know. But the problem doesn't mention anyone else making a call to Xiao Wang. So, we can't infer this.\n\nOption D: Xiao Wang answered the phone from everyone in the administration department. So, did Xiao Wang answer calls from everyone? Well, Xiao Wang called everyone, but did he receive calls from everyone? The information doesn't say that. It only says that Xiao Wang called everyone, but it doesn't say that everyone called Xiao Wang. So, we can't infer that Xiao Wang answered calls from everyone.\n\nSo, the only option that can be inferred is option B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
