      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to solve this logical reasoning problem. Let me read through the context and the question again to make sure I understand it properly.\n\nThe context says: \"Only when all countries in the world recognize the need to respect the sovereignty of any country and truly implement this treaty can the world be truly peaceful. However, because some countries hold a hegemonic attitude and adopt dual principles towards their own countries and other countries, they do not respect the sovereignty of some countries.\"\n\nSo, breaking this down, the first part is stating a condition for true peace. It says that only if every country respects the sovereignty of others and implements a treaty, then the world can be peaceful. The second part points out that some countries don't respect others' sovereignty because they have a hegemonic attitude and apply different principles to their own country versus others.\n\nNow, the question is asking which of the options can be seen based on this information. The options are A, B, C, D.\n\nLet me go through each option one by one.\n\nOption A: \"Every country should respect the sovereignty of other countries.\" The context does mention that respecting sovereignty is necessary for peace, but it also says that some countries don't do this. So, the context is more about the necessity rather than stating that every country currently does it. So, A is more of a recommendation or a condition rather than a fact based on the given information.\n\nOption B: \"At present, the world has achieved real peace.\" The context actually says the opposite. It implies that because some countries don't respect sovereignty, the world hasn't achieved true peace. So B is incorrect.\n\nOption C: \"A country with a hegemonic attitude is shameful.\" The context talks about countries having a hegemonic attitude and not respecting sovereignty, but it doesn't label such countries as shameful. It's more about their actions than their moral standing. So C might not be the best choice.\n\nOption D: \"At present, there is no real peace in the world.\" This aligns with the context. The first part says that only when all countries respect sovereignty can there be true peace. Since some don't, it means the world hasn't achieved real peace yet. So D seems correct.\n\nWait, let me double-check. The context says that because some countries don't respect sovereignty, the world can't be peaceful. So currently, since not all countries are respecting sovereignty, there's no real peace. Therefore, D is the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D",
