r is whether the two groups were similar at the start. If their skin was comparable before the experiment, then any differences after can be more confidently linked to the aspirin. Without that, there could be other variables affecting the results. So Option A seems to be the best support because it ensures that the initial conditions were the same, making the experiment's results more reliable.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
