f social shock where traditional and modern societies clash. Since developing countries are going through this process, it makes sense that they experience these shocks. So C seems correct because it directly relates to the information given.\n\nOption D: \"Developing countries began industrialization and modernization in an external environment completely different from developed countries.\" The context doesn't talk about the external environment or how industrialization started in developing versus developed countries. It only mentions that both have gone through the period of social shock. So D might not be correct because there's no information provided about the external environment differences.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the context supports option C because it directly relates to the social shocks experienced during the specified GNP range. The other options either make assumptions not supported by the context or aren't directly addressed.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C",
