ence. Therefore, the correct answer should be C.\n</think>\n\nThe text discusses how Puritanism influenced the development of modern science through its emphasis on the order of nature, the involvement of Puritans in scientific societies, and the inclusion of natural sciences in Puritan education. This indicates that religion, specifically Puritanism, had a promoting effect on science.\n\nThe correct option is: C",
