y more just, but it doesn't explicitly say that only strict rules can do this. It's more about the role of rules in guiding and regulating competition to achieve these societal goals.\n\nSo, the main content is about the emphasis on rules in competitions, which is option A. It's the central theme discussed in the text, covering both sports and the societal implications.\n</think>\n\nThe text emphasizes the importance of rules in competitions, highlighting their role in sports and broader societal contexts. The main focus is on how rules guide and regulate competition to achieve societal justice, with thinkers discussing their use. While fairness and social justice are mentioned, the core emphasis is on the rules themselves in competitions.\n\nThe correct option is: A",
