the crime rates. The mayor's argument is about crime rates, so this doesn't directly challenge the conclusion that the critics were wrong about crime increasing. It might make the reorganization look bad, but not the crime part.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the strongest challenge is Option B because it points out that the decrease in reports might not reflect actual crime rates but rather underreporting due to perceived unresponsiveness. This undermines the mayor's conclusion that the critics were wrong.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
