n- While the passage does talk about the importance of the economic system, it's more specific about the need to suppress negative externalities through the system. So this is a bit too broad.\n\nC) Honesty is both a social issue and an economic issue.\n- This is true because the passage discusses how personal morality (honesty) has social and economic implications. However, the main point is more about the system's role in managing these issues rather than just stating that honesty is both social and economic.\n\nD) System is needed to suppress negative externalities of dishonesty.\n- This directly addresses the passage's emphasis on the role of the economic system and governance mechanisms in restraining negative externalities caused by dishonesty. It aligns well with the main argument.\n\nSo, the most accurate summary is option D because it captures the essence of the passage, which is the necessity of a system to handle the negative effects of dishonesty, rather than just stating that honesty has broader implications or that the system is important in general.\n</think>\n\nThe passage emphasizes the importance of an economic system in managing the negative externalities caused by dishonesty, ensuring that those responsible bear the costs rather than society. The correct option is:\n\nThe correct option is: D",
