t solved it well, but at least most pay attention. So they are paying attention, but it doesn't say they are more than willing. It might imply they are trying, but not necessarily willing. So C might not be correct.\n\nOption D: Children's behavior of concealing their own situation has not attracted the attention of parents. The context says that the problem of concealing is not only worse solved but also not given enough attention. So yes, parents aren't paying enough attention to it. So D seems correct.\n\nWait, let me double-check. The context says that concealing is not only worse solved but also not given enough attention. So D is correct because it states that the behavior hasn't attracted enough attention from parents.\n\nSo the correct answer should be D.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D",
