bing and learning from foreign theories, it's more about testing their effectiveness and then creating a system. D seems more about openness and talent, which isn't the main focus.\n\nSo, putting it together, the passage is about testing Western theories empirically, keeping what works, and then developing a new system. Option C mentions eliminating impurities (testing) and independent innovation, which aligns well with the main idea.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C",
