e less effective for men and for less time. So D directly addresses the effectiveness of the same painkillers. B is more about the timing of when the pain returns, which is a consequence of the painkillers being less effective. But the question is about the meaning of the expression, which is about the effectiveness of the painkillers. So D seems to be the more accurate interpretation.\n\nWait, but the question is about the meaning of the expression, which is the statement given. So the statement is that men experienced less pain relief and the painkillers were less effective for less time. So the main point is that the same painkillers worked better for women. Therefore, D is the correct answer.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D",
