should be doing\u2014cultivating the ability to discover and create, rather than just imparting standard answers. Therefore, the subject is likely the purpose of education.\n\nLet me check the options again. Option D is \"The purpose of education,\" which seems to fit because the passage is discussing what education should aim to do, emphasizing discovery and creativity over rote learning.\n\nI think that makes sense. The passage is making a point about education's role in fostering discovery, so the subject is the purpose of education.\n</think>\n\nThe passage discusses the essence of knowledge, the role of intellectuals, and the purpose of education, but it primarily focuses on the latter. It argues that education should cultivate creativity and discovery rather than just imparting standard answers. Therefore, the subject is the purpose of education.\n\nThe correct option is: D",
