illegal acts are criminal, and only criminal acts are sanctioned. So, unless we know that Huang Tao's illegal acts are specifically criminal, we can't say for sure they'll be sanctioned. Therefore, C might not be necessarily true.\n\nOption D: All actions sanctioned by criminal law are criminal actions.\n\nStatement 1 says that all criminal acts are sanctioned. But it doesn't say anything about whether only criminal acts are sanctioned. It's possible that some non-criminal acts are also sanctioned. So, D is making a stronger claim than what's given. Therefore, D isn't necessarily true.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the only option that must be true is A.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
