d is greatly affected by the time spent eating. The context doesn't mention anything about the duration of eating, only the number of meals and the total amount. So D isn't supported by the information provided.\n\nPutting it all together, the context supports the idea that most people eat more when they eat more often, which means their total food intake increases. Therefore, increasing the number of meals doesn't lead to a reduction in cholesterol because they're consuming more food. So the correct answer should be B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
