      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to solve this logic problem. Let me read through the context and question again to make sure I understand everything.\n\nWe have a class that needs to form a group of five students: two girls and three boys. The girls are Fang Rufen, Guo Yanran, and He Zhilian. The boys are Peng Youwen, Qiu Zhijie, Ren Xiangyang, Song Wenkai, and Tang Xiaohua.\n\nThere are three requirements:\n1. Guo Yanran and Tang Xiaohua cannot be selected at the same time.\n2. Peng Youwen and Song Wenkai cannot be selected at the same time.\n3. Qiu Zhijie and Tang Xiaohua cannot be selected at the same time.\n\nThe question is: If Tang Xiaohua is selected, which two of the following must be selected? The options are A, B, C, D.\n\nSo, the first thing I need to do is figure out what happens when Tang Xiaohua is selected. Let's break down each requirement step by step.\n\nStarting with requirement 1: Guo Yanran and Tang Xiaohua cannot be selected together. Since Tang Xiaohua is selected, Guo Yanran cannot be selected. So, Guo Yanran is out. That leaves us with two girls: Fang Rufen and He Zhilian. Since we need to select two girls, both of them must be selected. So, Fang Rufen and He Zhilian are definitely in the group.\n\nNow, moving on to the boys. We need to select three boys. Tang Xiaohua is already selected, so that's one spot. Now, let's look at the other requirements.\n\nRequirement 3 says Qiu Zhijie and Tang Xiaohua can't be selected together. Since Tang Xiaohua is selected, Qiu Zhijie can't be selected. So, Qiu Zhijie is out. That leaves us with Peng Youwen, Ren Xiangyang, and Song Wenkai as the remaining boys to choose from.\n\nBut wait, requirement 2 says Peng Youwen and Song Wenkai can't be selected together. So, we have to choose between them. Since we need three boys and Tang Xiaohua is already one, we need two more from the remaining boys. But since Qiu Zhijie is out, the available boys are Peng Youwen, Ren Xiangyang, and Song Wenkai.\n\nWait, no, that's not right. Let me correct that. The boys are Peng Youwen, Qiu Zhijie, Ren Xiangyang, Song Wenkai, and Tang Xiaohua. Since Tang is selected, Qiu is out. So, the remaining boys are Peng, Ren, and Song. But we need to select three boys, so we have to choose all three? Wait, no, because we already have Tang, so we need two more from Peng, Ren, Song.\n\nBut requirement 2 says Peng and Song can't be together. So, we can't have both Peng and Song. Therefore, we have to choose either Peng or Song, but not both. So, let's see: if we choose Peng, then we can't choose Song, so the third boy would have to be Ren. Similarly, if we choose Song, we can't choose Peng, so the third boy would be Ren. So, in either case, Ren Xiangyang must be selected because we need two more boys, and we can't have both Peng and Song.\n\nWait, but let me think again. We have to select three boys, and Tang is already one. So, we need two more from Peng, Ren, Song. But since Peng and Song can't be together, we can only choose one of them. So, the two boys would be either Peng and Ren, or Song and Ren. So, in both cases, Ren is selected. Therefore, Ren Xiangyang must be selected.\n\nBut wait, the question is about which two must be selected, not necessarily all three. So, the two girls are Fang and He, as we determined earlier. So, the two girls must be selected, which are Fang Rufen and He Zhilian. So, looking at the options, option D is Fang Rufen and He Zhilian.\n\nWait, but let me make sure I'm not missing anything. The question is asking which two must be selected if Tang Xiaohua is selected. So, the two girls are definitely selected because Guo is excluded, so Fang and He are the only options. So, the correct answer should be D.\n\nBut let me double-check the boys. Since Tang is selected, Qiu is out. So, the boys available are Peng, Ren, Song. We need two more. But Peng and Song can't be together, so we have to choose either Peng or Song, plus Ren. So, Ren is definitely selected, but either Peng or Song is selected, not both. So, the two boys selected would be Tang, Ren, and either Peng or Song. So, the two girls are Fang and He, so the two that must be selected are Fang and He.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D) Fang rufen and he zhilian",
