revious arrangement, option D was false. So, depending on which brands are equal, option D can be true or false.\n\nBut the question is asking which statement must be inconsistent, meaning it's always false regardless of the arrangement.\n\nSo, in the first arrangement (B = C), option D is false.\n\nIn the second arrangement (E = C), option D is true.\n\nTherefore, option D is not necessarily inconsistent because it can be true in some arrangements.\n\nOn the other hand, option B: A and C have the same power consumption.\n\nIn the first arrangement (B = C), A < C, so A \u2260 C.\n\nIn the second arrangement (E = C), A < C, so A \u2260 C.\n\nSo, in both possible arrangements, A \u2260 C. Therefore, option B is always inconsistent because it's impossible for A and C to have the same power consumption.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is option B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
