veral years for a city to mature and for popularity (population) to gather, which is exactly what option C is saying.\n\nOption D: \"Large cities have large populations and are well matured.\" While this is a general statement, the context doesn't specifically talk about city size but rather the time it takes to develop. Also, the context uses Shenzhen as an example, which is a large city but still considered unfinished because it's not yet mature. So this might not be the best support.\n\nSo, putting it all together, option C directly supports the idea that cities take time to develop and gather population, leading to maturity, which is exactly what the context is emphasizing.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C",
