      "index": 0,
      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out the main idea of the passage provided. Let me read through it again to make sure I understand it properly.\n\nThe passage talks about how the network (I think they're referring to the internet or online networks) not only discovers problems but also acts as a clue provider and supervisor to solve them. It mentions that compared to other supervision and management mechanisms, the network's supervision ability is more advanced. It seems like the network often exposes problem clues before they're officially investigated and solved.\n\nHowever, the passage then cautions that while network supervision is effective now, it's not a normal or mainstream way of supervision in a society governed by the rule of law. It emphasizes that we shouldn't rely on the network as the main method of supervision. Instead, the focus should be on how to fully utilize the original supervision mechanisms, which is an urgent problem.\n\nSo, the main points are:\n1. Network supervision is advanced and effective.\n2. Despite its effectiveness, it's not a normal or mainstream method in a lawful society.\n3. The original supervision mechanisms need to be utilized more effectively.\n\nNow, looking at the options:\n\nA) The society ruled by law cannot mainly rely on the network for effective supervision.\nB) The network has more advanced supervision ability than other supervision mechanisms.\nC) Network supervision can play a better role on the basis of self-improvement.\nD) An important way of supervision in today's society is network supervision.\n\nOption B seems to directly state that the network is more advanced, which is true according to the passage. But the main idea isn't just about the network's ability; it's about not relying on it as the main method. So B might be a supporting point but not the main idea.\n\nOption D says network supervision is an important way, which is also true, but again, the passage is cautioning against it becoming the main method. So D might be a bit misleading because it's presented as an important way, but the passage is more about not making it the primary method.\n\nOption C talks about network supervision improving itself to play a better role. The passage doesn't mention anything about the network needing to improve; it's more about the existing mechanisms needing to be utilized.\n\nOption A states that a lawful society can't mainly rely on the network. This aligns with the passage's caution that network supervision isn't a normal or mainstream method and that the original mechanisms should be the focus. So A seems to capture the main idea.\n\nI think the main idea is that while the network is good, it shouldn't be the main way of supervision in a lawful society. Therefore, the correct answer should be A.\n</think>\n\nThe passage emphasizes that although network supervision is effective, it should not be the primary method in a lawful society. It highlights the need to focus on existing supervision mechanisms. \n\nThe correct option is: A",
