n language and emotion. Then it goes on to talk about the book helping beginners. So which is the main focus?\n\nThe first sentence sets the stage, but the rest of the text is more about the book and its role in helping beginners. So maybe the main content is about the book providing help, making option C the answer. But wait, option B is about the process of creation, which is the initial point. However, the text spends more time discussing the book's role, so perhaps the main content is about the book helping beginners.\n\nAlternatively, the first sentence could be the main idea, with the rest explaining how the book supports that process. But I think the focus shifts to the book as the solution for beginners, so option C might be the main content.\n\nWait, let me read the question again: \"which of the followings is the main content of this text?\" The text starts by explaining the process, then introduces the book as a solution. So the main content is about the book providing help, making option C correct. But option B is also a key point. Hmm, I'm a bit confused.\n\nWait, the first sentence is a general statement, but the rest is about the book. So the main content is about the book helping beginners, so option C is correct. But I'm not entirely sure because the first sentence is a fundamental point. Maybe the main content is the process, but I think the text is more focused on the book's role.\n</think>\n\nThe text primarily discusses how the book \"Tang and Song Poetry Rhythms\" assists beginners in poetry creation by providing guidance on words, rhymes, and rhetorical devices. While it mentions the process of mutual accommodation between language and emotion, the focus is on the book's role. \n\nThe correct option is: C",
