ive, so again, it's a food material. Even if it's excessive and harmful, it's still a food additive. The crime is about using non-food materials, so this might not fit. Unless the coloring is a non-food material, but I think it's considered a food additive, so it's still a food material.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Option A is the clear fit because industrial alcohol is a non-food, toxic material used in food production and sold. The others either use food materials (even if problematic) or involve issues other than non-food toxic materials.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
