w, let's summarize all possible scenarios.\n\nFrom Case 1:\n\nSubcase 1a: B on Tuesday.\n\nSubcase 1b: B on Monday or Wednesday.\n\nSubcase 1c: B on Monday or Tuesday.\n\nFrom Case 2:\n\nSubcase 2b: B on Monday.\n\nSubcase 2c: B on Monday or Tuesday.\n\nWait, but in Subcase 1b, when A is on Tuesday and D on Thursday, B can be on Monday or Wednesday.\n\nIn Subcase 1c, when A is on Wednesday and D on Friday, B can be on Monday or Tuesday.\n\nIn Subcase 2b, when D is on Tuesday and A on Thursday, B is on Monday.\n\nIn Subcase 2c, when D is on Wednesday and A on Friday, B can be on Monday or Tuesday.\n\nSo, compiling all possible days for B:\n\nFrom Subcase 1a: Tuesday.\n\nFrom Subcase 1b: Monday, Wednesday.\n\nFrom Subcase 1c: Monday, Tuesday.\n\nFrom Subcase 2b: Monday.\n\nFrom Subcase 2c: Monday, Tuesday.\n\nSo B can be on Monday, Tuesday, or Wednesday.\n\nBut wait, let's check if all these are possible without conflicts.\n\nWait, in Subcase 1b, when A is on Tuesday and D on Thursday, B can be on Monday or Wednesday.\n\nIf B is on Wednesday, then:\n\nA: Tuesday\n\nB: Wednesday\n\nD: Thursday\n\nC and E on Monday and Friday.\n\nBut C can't be on Tuesday, which is fine.\n\nBut let's check if B is before D and E. B is on Wednesday, D on Thursday, and E on Friday. So yes, B is before both.\n\nBut wait, in this case, C would be on Monday or Friday. If C is on Monday, that's fine. If C is on Friday, that's also fine.\n\nSo B can be on Wednesday in this scenario.\n\nSimilarly, in Subcase 1c, when A is on Wednesday and D on Friday, B can be on Monday or Tuesday.\n\nIf B is on Tuesday, then:\n\nA: Wednesday\n\nB: Tuesday\n\nD: Friday\n\nC and E on Monday and Thursday.\n\nBut wait, B is on Tuesday, which is before A on Wednesday, which is okay because the requirement is that B is before D and E, not necessarily before A.\n\nWait, no, the requirement is that B is before D and E, but A can be anywhere else. So that's fine.\n\nBut let's check if this assignment works.\n\nSo:\n\nA