      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which company David should choose between Huizhong and Cantor. Let me start by understanding the salary structures of both companies.\n\nFirst, Huizhong offers a half-year salary of $500,000 with an increase of $50,000 per half-year. That means every six months, David's salary goes up by $50k. On the other hand, Cantor offers an annual salary of $1 million with an annual increase of $200,000. So, every year, Cantor adds $200k to his salary.\n\nI think the best way to compare these is to calculate the total salary David would receive over a two-year period from both companies. That way, I can see which option gives him more money overall.\n\nStarting with Huizhong:\n\n- The first half-year: $500,000\n- The second half-year: $500k + $50k = $550k\n- The third half-year: $550k + $50k = $600k\n- The fourth half-year: $600k + $50k = $650k\n\nSo, over two years (which is four half-years), the total would be $500k + $550k + $600k + $650k. Let me add those up:\n\n500,000 + 550,000 = 1,050,000\n1,050,000 + 600,000 = 1,650,000\n1,650,000 + 650,000 = 2,300,000\n\nSo, Huizhong pays a total of $2,300,000 over two years.\n\nNow, Cantor's offer:\n\n- First year: $1,000,000\n- Second year: $1,000k + $200k = $1,200k\n\nTotal over two years: $1,000,000 + $1,200,000 = $2,200,000\n\nComparing the two totals: Huizhong gives $2,300,000 and Cantor gives $2,200,000. So, Huizhong is better by $100,000 over two years.\n\nWait, but let me check if I did that correctly. Because sometimes when salaries are given per half-year, the annual salary might be different. Let me think again.\n\nWait, Huizhong's first half-year is $500k, so the first year would be $500k + $550k = $1,050k. The second year would be $600k + $650k = $1,250k. So total is $1,050k + $1,250k = $2,300k, which matches what I had before.\n\nCantor's first year is $1,000k, second year $1,200k, total $2,200k.\n\nSo, over two years, Huizhong pays $100k more. That means David would earn an extra $100k by choosing Huizhong.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) David will go to Cantor because he'll get an extra $150k in two years. That's not correct because Huizhong pays more.\n\nB) David will go to Huizhong because he'll get an extra $50k a year. Wait, over two years, it's $100k extra, so per year that's $50k. So this option says he gets an extra $50k a year, which is correct.\n\nC) David will go to Cantor because he'll have an extra $50k a year. No, because Huizhong is better.\n\nD) David will go to Huizhong because he'll have an extra $70k a year. That doesn't match because it's $50k extra per year.\n\nSo the correct answer should be option B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B) David will go to huizhong because he will get an extra $50,000 a year.",
