 risk from fibers being released, not specifically about the workers. So this might be a side point and not directly strengthen the main argument about the fibers being released into the environment.\n\nOption D: Asbestos poses far less risk than smoking, drugs, alcohol, diet, or lack of exercise. This is comparing asbestos to other risks. The argument is that removing it is bad because it releases fibers. If this option is true, it might actually weaken the argument because it's saying asbestos isn't that bad compared to other things. So the government might not need to worry as much, but the argument is against removal because of the risk. So this might not help.\n\nSo, putting it together, Option B seems to strengthen the argument the most because it points out that even after removal, there's a risk of disturbance, which supports the idea that removal isn't a good solution.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
