      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the options A to D fits the definition of field dependence given in the context. Let me start by understanding what field dependence means. The context says that field dependence involves using external references as the basis for processing information. This means that people with this trait find it hard to ignore environmental factors. Their attitudes and self-perception are easily influenced by others, especially authorities. They're good at observing words and emotions and focus on remembering social content in verbal messages.\n\nSo, field dependence is about being externally oriented. People who are field dependent rely on external cues and are influenced by their surroundings and others' opinions, particularly those in authority. They pay attention to social aspects and are swayed by others' words and emotions.\n\nNow, looking at the options:\n\nA) Have the ability to learn independently. This sounds more like an internal trait, maybe field independence. If someone can learn on their own, they're not relying on external factors as much.\n\nB) Have one's own opinion on the evaluation of others. This suggests that the person has their own perspective, which might mean they're not easily swayed by others' evaluations. So this might be field independent.\n\nC) Doing things is dominated by intrinsic motivation. Intrinsic motivation comes from within, so this is about internal drives, not external influences. So this is likely field independent.\n\nD) Doing things is dominated by external motivation. External motivation means the person is driven by outside factors, such as rewards, recognition, or others' opinions. This aligns with field dependence because they're influenced by external factors.\n\nSo, putting it all together, field dependence is about being externally influenced, so the correct answer should be D.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: D",
