n is formed in planets, that implies that planets existed before the universe was two billion years old. So B is correct.\n\nOption D says the planet with time is not the same as the gas cloud. Well, planets and gas clouds are different, but the context doesn't directly state that. It just says that when planets explode, they disperse elements into gas clouds. So D is a true statement, but it's more of a general fact rather than something directly inferred from the context.\n\nSo between B and D, B is more directly supported by the context. Therefore, the correct answer is B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
