nthetic pesticides have simpler chemical structures than natural drugs. The context mentions that natural drugs are complex. If synthetic ones are simpler, maybe they're more easily broken down or less toxic. But wait, the argument is that because people are used to complex natural toxins, synthetic ones aren't a big deal. If synthetic are simpler, maybe they're less harmful, which would support the argument. Alternatively, maybe simpler structures could mean they're more effective or more toxic. I'm not sure yet. I'll come back to this.\n\nOption D: Natural drugs target specific organisms, while synthetic pesticides harm many. This could be a problem because if synthetic pesticides affect a broader range of organisms, including humans, that would mean they're more harmful, which undermines the argument that they don't cause much new harm.\n\nSo, the argument is that synthetic pesticides aren't much worse because people are already dealing with natural ones. If synthetic are more concentrated (A), that's bad. If they're simpler (C), maybe that's good or bad. If they affect more organisms (D), that's bad. If humans have adapted (B), that's good.\n\nWait, the question is which option does NOT undermine the argument. So, the correct answer is the one that doesn't weaken the argument.\n\nOption B actually supports the argument, so it doesn't undermine it. The others (A, C, D) could potentially undermine it.\n\nWait, but let me think again. The argument is that because people are ingesting natural drugs without harm, synthetic pesticides don't cause much new harm. So, if synthetic pesticides are more concentrated (A), that could mean they're more harmful, which would undermine the argument. If they have simpler structures (C), maybe they're less complex, so perhaps they're less toxic, which would support the argument. Alternatively, simpler structures might mean they're more easily absorbed or more potent, which could be bad. I'm not sure. But the context says natural drugs are complex, so maybe synthetic being simpler is less of a problem. Or maybe the complexity is what makes them safe because they're harder to metabolize. Hmm, not sure.\n\nOption D says synthetic pesticides affect more organisms, which could include humans, making them more harmful, thus undermining the argument.\n\nSo, the options that undermine the argument are A, C, D. The one that doesn't is B because it supports the argument.\n\nWait, but the question is which does NOT undermine. So the correct answer is B.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
