      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I'm trying to figure out the correct answer to this question about the meaning of \"contextual\" in the given paragraph. Let me read through the context again to make sure I understand it properly.\n\nThe context says: \"Rural culture is a set of contextual production and life experience system, which is determined by the production and living conditions of the society. In any case, the import of advanced culture from the outside to such a society is divorced from reality.\"\n\nHmm, so the key term here is \"contextual.\" I need to figure out what that means in this specific context. The question is asking which option best captures the meaning of \"contextual\" as used in the paragraph.\n\nLet me break it down. The first sentence mentions that rural culture is a \"contextual production and life experience system.\" It's determined by the production and living conditions of the society. So, \"contextual\" here seems to relate to the specific conditions or environment of the rural society.\n\nThe second sentence talks about importing advanced culture from outside, which is \"divorced from reality.\" That suggests that bringing in external cultures doesn't fit well with the existing rural context because it's not connected to their actual situation.\n\nSo, putting it together, \"contextual\" probably means that rural culture is connected to and integrated with the local reality. It's not just any culture but one that's tied to the specific conditions of the rural society.\n\nLooking at the options:\n\nA) Adapted to the experience of production and life in various parts of the countryside.\n- This seems related because it's about adapting to production and life experiences, which are part of the context.\n\nB) Adapting to the actual development and changes in rural areas.\n- This is about adapting to changes, which might be a bit more about evolution rather than being connected to the existing context.\n\nC) Connected with and integrated with the reality of the local rural society.\n- This directly mentions being connected and integrated with the local reality, which aligns with the idea that rural culture is determined by its own conditions.\n\nD) Adapted to the development of advanced culture.\n- This seems to refer to external advanced culture, which the paragraph says is disconnected, so this might not be the right fit.\n\nComparing A and C, both seem relevant. However, the paragraph emphasizes that rural culture is determined by its own production and living conditions, making it connected to the local reality. Option C directly states this connection and integration, which seems more precise than option A, which is more about adaptation across different parts of the countryside.\n\nSo, I think the best answer is C.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: C",
