ange its approach to survive, which is exactly what option D is saying.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the main idea is about how traditional Chinese culture forced Buddhism to adapt its strategies. Therefore, the correct answer should be D.\n</think>\n\nThe passage discusses how Buddhism had to adapt to Chinese culture by altering its teachings, such as emphasizing filial piety, to survive. This adaptation was a response to the strong influence of Chinese traditional culture. \n\nThe correct option is: D",
