ort the idea that blue spaces themselves are beneficial. It's more of a background reason rather than a direct support for the conclusion about blue spaces.\n\nWait, but the conclusion is that blue spaces are beneficial. So if B is saying that urban environments are bad, it indirectly supports the need for blue spaces, but it doesn't provide evidence that blue spaces are good. So it doesn't directly support the conclusion. Therefore, B is the option that doesn't support the conclusion.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: B",
