      "text": "<think>\nOkay, so I need to figure out which of the options A, B, C, or D is correct based on the given context about monosodium glutamate (MSG). Let me read through the context again carefully to understand the points made.\n\nThe context starts by saying that MSG is a family essential product but has been questioned recently. It mentions that adding MSG during cooking is proposed to have a great harmful effect on the human body. The harmful effects listed include hair loss, vision loss, zinc deficiency, and even cancer or other visceral diseases. However, the context also states that according to research, MSG can enhance people's appetite, improve the body's ability to absorb other things, and has a certain tonic effect.\n\nSo, the context presents both negative and positive viewpoints about MSG. It's important to note that the negative effects are presented as proposed or suggested, while the positive effects are stated as findings from research.\n\nNow, looking at the options:\n\nOption A: \"Adding monosodium glutamate during cooking may have a great harmful effect on the human body.\" The context does mention that it's been proposed that adding MSG has a great harmful effect. So this seems to align with the first part of the context.\n\nOption B: \"Msg may cause cancer or other visceral diseases.\" The context does list cancer and other visceral diseases as potential effects, but it's under the proposed harmful effects. So this could be correct, but I need to check the other options.\n\nOption C: \"Monosodium glutamate can improve people's food and martial arts, and has a certain tonic effect on the human body.\" Wait, the context says it improves the ability to absorb other things and has a tonic effect, but it doesn't mention martial arts. Also, \"improve people's food\" might not be the right phrasing. The context says it enhances appetite and improves absorption, so this option might not be accurate.\n\nOption D: \"Monosodium glutamate is sa