ne who didn't vote for all three candidates.\n\nSo if someone didn't vote for all three, Li Zilu voted for them.\n\nNow, let's consider each person:\n\n- Zhang Hao didn't vote for anyone, so he didn't vote for all three. Therefore, Li Zilu voted for Zhang Hao.\n\n- Wang Ming: If Wang Ming didn't vote for all three, then Li Zilu voted for him. If he did vote for all three, Li Zilu didn't vote for him.\n\n- Li Zilu himself: If he didn't vote for all three, then Li Zilu voted for himself. If he did vote for all three, he didn't vote for himself.\n\nNow, let's see what we can deduce.\n\nFirst, Zhang Hao didn't vote for anyone, so Li Zilu voted for him.\n\nNow, let's consider Wang Ming. If Wang Ming voted for Zhao Jie, then he would have to vote for everyone who voted for Zhao Jie, including himself if he did. So if Wang Ming voted for Zhao Jie, he would have to vote for himself, which would mean he voted for Zhao Jie and himself. But does that mean he voted for all three? Not necessarily, unless he also voted for Li Zilu.\n\nWait, but if Wang Ming voted for Zhao Jie, he would have to vote for everyone who voted for Zhao Jie. So if Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie, Wang Ming would have to vote for Li Zilu as well.\n\nBut let's think about whether Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie.\n\nLi Zilu's rule is that he voted for everyone who didn't vote for all three. So if someone didn't vote for all three, Li Zilu voted for them.\n\nNow, let's consider whether Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie.\n\nIf Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie, then he must have voted for everyone who didn't vote for all three. So if someone didn't vote for all three, Li Zilu voted for them.\n\nBut if Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie, that would mean he voted for Zhao Jie, but we don't know if he voted for all three or not.\n\nWait, perhaps it's better to consider whether Wang Ming and Li Zilu voted for each other.\n\nLet me try to see:\n\nIf Wang Ming voted for Li Zilu, then according to his rule, he must have voted for everyone who voted for Zhao Jie. So if Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie, then Wang Ming would have to vote for Li Zilu.\n\nBut if Li Zilu didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then Wang Ming wouldn't have to vote for him.\n\nAlternatively, if Wang Ming didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then he wouldn't have to vote for anyone, so he didn't vote for Li Zilu.\n\nBut let's think about Li Zilu's behavior. He voted for everyone who didn't vote for all three.\n\nSo if Wang Ming didn't vote for all three, Li Zilu voted for him.\n\nIf Wang Ming did vote for all three, Li Zilu didn't vote for him.\n\nNow, let's consider whether Wang Ming voted for all three.\n\nIf Wang Ming voted for Zhao Jie, then he would have to vote for everyone who voted for Zhao Jie. So if someone else voted for Zhao Jie, he would have to vote for them.\n\nBut if he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then he wouldn't have to vote for anyone else.\n\nWait, but if he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then he didn't have to vote for anyone, so his vote set W would be empty.\n\nBut if he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, so he didn't have to vote for anyone else. So W would be empty.\n\nBut if W is empty, then he didn't vote for anyone, including Zhao Jie, so he didn't have to vote for anyone else.\n\nWait, but if he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then he didn't have to vote for anyone else, so W is empty.\n\nBut if W is empty, then he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, so he didn't have to vote for anyone else.\n\nBut then, if W is empty, then he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, so he didn't have to vote for anyone else.\n\nBut then, if he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then he didn't have to vote for anyone else, so W is empty.\n\nWait, but if W is empty, then he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, so he didn't have to vote for anyone else.\n\nBut then, if he didn't vote for Zhao Jie, then he didn't have to vote for anyone else, so W is empty.\n\nWait, this seems a bit circular. Let me try to approach it differently.\n\nLet me consider whether Wang Ming voted for Zhao Jie