n\nThen T is seventh. T can be red or green. If T is red, then S (green) and T (red) are okay.\n\nBut let's check the consecutive rule:\n\nX (red), Z (green) \u2013 okay.\n\nZ (green), U (red) \u2013 okay.\n\nU (red), Y (green) \u2013 okay.\n\nY (green), W (red) \u2013 okay.\n\nW (red), S (green) \u2013 okay.\n\nS (green), T (red) \u2013 okay.\n\nSo no consecutive reds. That works.\n\nAlso, Y is before T and W. Y is fourth, W is fifth, T is seventh. So Y is before both, which is correct.\n\nZ is before U, correct.\n\nS is sixth, correct.\n\nSo Option A fits all the conditions.\n</think>\n\nThe correct option is: A",
